<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ s/adj GDP rises 0.7 pct in December qtr.</title>
<headline>NZ s/adj GDP rises 0.7 pct in December qtr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Thursday released the following estimates of New Zealand's real, production-based gross domestic product for the quarter ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Economists estimated GDP would rise a seasonally adjusted 0.4 percent for the quarter for an annual rise of 2.3 percent.</p>
<p>Quarter-on-quarter seasonally-adjusted figures (revised-from figures in brackets):</p>
<p>    Dec 1996		   Sept 1996		  Dec 1995</p>
<p>    0.7 pct		    0.8 pct (0.6)	    0.4 pct (0.5)</p>
<p>S/adj change at constant prices from yr-ago quarter  </p>
<p>    Dec 1996		   Sept 1996		  Dec 1995</p>
<p>    2.9 pct		    2.7 pct (2.2)	    2.4 pct (2.3)</p>
<p>Actual annual change</p>
<p>    Dec 1996		   Sept 1996		  Dec 1995</p>
<p>    2.7 pct		    2.5 pct (2.3)	    3.5 pct (3.4)</p>
<p>Quarterly contributions to GDP movements (percent)</p>
<p>				   Dec 1996	   Sept 1996</p>
<p>    Agriculture		    1.9		-1.3</p>
<p>    Fishing, forestry, mining -7.7		 6.4</p>
<p>    Manufacturing		  1.4		 1.7</p>
<p>    Power, gas, water	    5.8		-2.6</p>
<p>    Construction		   2.4		-0.7</p>
<p>    Restaurants, hotels	 -1.2		 1.0</p>
<p>    Dwellings			0.4		 0.4</p>
<p>    Transport, Communications  2.4		 1.6</p>
<p>    Govt services		  0.7		-0.3</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
